# pins.env -- the FLEET pins, shipped inside the published
# @nine-at-a-time-media/skills payload (tds-utils
# docs/design/SANDBOX-LIFECYCLE.DESIGN.md, D1).
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ROLLOUT LEVER for the fleet executables. The acquire
# engine (tds-utils lmde/lib/acquire.sh; vendored copy in template-tools
# packages/naatm-sandbox/lib/acquire.sh) installs the skills package first
# (floating) and then, when no explicit --pins file was passed, reads THIS
# file from the installed payload
# (~/.local/lib/node_modules/@nine-at-a-time-media/skills/pins.env) to pin
# the executable packages. Because the skills package publishes on every
# merge to main, a pin bump here is a reviewed PR that reaches every
# surface on its NEXT SESSION -- no environment rebuild, no re-paste, no
# cache wait. The merge is the rollout; the PR is the review gate
# (ai-tools#72: a default-branch push never grants execution in consumers
# by itself -- consumers install the pinned, registry-integrity-checked
# published version this file names).
#
# Resolution order per package (D1): explicit --pins argument > this file >
# float to registry latest. Plain KEY="value" assignments only -- no logic,
# no command substitution. An absent or UNSET key floats that package.
#
# THERE IS NO SKILLS_VERSION KEY, deliberately. The engine never applied
# this file to the skills row anyway -- pinning the payload from inside the
# payload being installed is a self-reference -- so the key documented a
# lever that did not exist. The skills row always floats: a skill merge IS
# the rollout. For an emergency skills freeze, pass an explicit --pins file
# with SKILLS_VERSION set; that path is unchanged and still works.
#
# To bump: `npm view @nine-at-a-time-media/<pkg> version
# --registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com` (classic read:packages token
# required) reports the published latest; set it here and land via PR.

# clai (executable: pinned version, npm registry integrity). 0.8.0 is the
# first release cut AFTER the package-first source order landed
# (tds-utils#190): provision prefers the acquired skills payload over the
# wheel's bundled _data fallback.
CLAI_VERSION="0.8.0"

# ast-mcp (executable MCP server). 0.4.0 is the published latest as of
# 2026-08-13 (the 0.3.x pins that sat frozen in environment snapshots are
# exactly the staleness class D1 removes -- tds-utils#194).
AST_MCP_VERSION="0.4.0"

# gadmin (@nine-at-a-time-media/admin; the npm name is `admin`, the binary
# is `gadmin` -- tds-utils#186).
ADMIN_VERSION="0.4.0"

# git-mirror: NOT PUBLISHED to GitHub Packages as of 2026-08-13 (npm view
# fails). UNSET floats it, which degrades fail-open with a warning until it
# is published (tds-utils#188).
GIT_MIRROR_VERSION="UNSET"
